e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277184" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277184" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277184" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "<"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277184" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277184" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-75991" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution of $-{x}^{2}-3x+4<0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-75991" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}-3x+4<0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=-{x}^{2}-3x+4\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-3x+4 & =0 \\\\ -({x}^{2}+3x-4) & =0 \\\\ -(x+4)(x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=-4$ and $x=1,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/6a5528147c994e180c2ffb41bd259dae489a3fc02fa1d6c77452d6cf1722e9be.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x<-4$ or $x>1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-75991" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50c6f502bd60fceea6148813148952d7c9f32825dff9e7c7a62692e856f6f20d"} {"question" "q-75991" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-75991" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1<x<4"] ["math" "-4<x<1"] ["math" "1<x<4"] ["text" "$x<-1$ or $x>4$"] ["text" "$x<-4$ or $x>1$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "fi