s of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-{x}^{2}+4x$ lies above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+4x & =0 \\\\ -x(x-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=0$ and $x=4,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/d234c29de2a39c664d6a03acf1d8cc43782914a3c82045cc103353ebaf67b897.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}+4x\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $0\\le x\\le 4.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [0,4].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-3881" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50c6f502bd60fceea6148813148952d7c9f32825dff9e7c7a62692e856f6f20d"} {"question" "q-3881" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-3881" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-4]\\cup [0,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,0]\\cup [4,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in [-4,0]"] ["math" "x\\in [-4,4]"] ["math" "x\\in [0,4]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-3881" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\in [0,4]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-44772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution of $-2{x}^{2}\\ge 5x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-44772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2} & \\ge 5x \\\\ -2{x}^{2}-5x & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-2{x}^{2}-5x$ lies above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}-5x & =0 \\\\ -x(2x+5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-\\frac{5}{2}$ and $x=0,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/33b031b579d84d633e4dcc56c912333327449fcbc6969eeceb34e209c4d308d1.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}-5x\\ge 0,\n$$\n\n we look for the part of the parabola that is above the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\n Based on the graph, the solution is $-\\frac{5}{2}\\le x\\le 0.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [-\\frac{5}{2},0].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-44772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50c6f502bd60fceea6148813148952d7c9f32825dff9e7c7a62692e856f6f20d"} {"question" "q-44772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-44772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-\\frac{5}{2}]\\cup [0,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,0]\\cup [\\frac{5}{2},\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in [-\\frac{5}{2},0]"] ["math" "x\\in [0,3]"] ["math" "x\\in [0,\\frac{5}{2}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-44772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\in [-\\frac{5}{2},0]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-3951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution of $2{x}^{2}-12\\le -5x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-3951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-12 & \\le -5x \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+5x-12 & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=2{x}^{2}+5x-12$ lies below the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+5x-12 & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}+8x)+(-3x-12) & =0 \\\\ 2x(x+4)-3(x+4) & =0 \\\\ (2x-3)(x+4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-4$ and $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/ba6c384800a5b42f2033527997328aa9f9d792b33b3fabecfe9b3a93789f46c4.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving\n \n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}+5x-12\\le 0,\n$$\n\n we look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\n Based on the graph, the solution is $-4\\le x\\le \\frac{3}{2}.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [-4,\\frac{3}{2}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-3951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50c6f502bd60fceea6148813148952d7c9f32825dff9e7c7a62692e856f6f20d"} {"question" "q-3951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"que