 in solving \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+9x\\le 0,\n$$\n\n we look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-9\\le x\\le 0.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [-9,0].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-3875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50c6f502bd60fceea6148813148952d7c9f32825dff9e7c7a62692e856f6f20d"} {"question" "q-3875" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-3875" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-9]\\cup [0,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,9]\\cup [0,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in [-9,0]"] ["math" "x\\in [-9,9]"] ["math" "x\\in [0,9]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-3875" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\in [-9,0]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-3878" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}<3x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-3878" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & <3x \\\\ {x}^{2}-3x & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y={x}^{2}-3x$ lies below the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-3x & =0 \\\\ x(x-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=0$ and $x=3,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/a341979142ef569d7ba4ec5b44178e8b4e4374fa9294e4664ae0f0008b76caab.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving\n \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-3x<0,\n$$\n\n we look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $0<x<3.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (0,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-3878" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50c6f502bd60fceea6148813148952d7c9f32825dff9e7c7a62692e856f6f20d"} {"question" "q-3878" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-3878" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (0,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (3,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in (0,3)"] ["math" "x\\in (0,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-3878" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\in (0,3)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $-2{x}^{2}>10x+12$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2} & >10x+12 \\\\ -2{x}^{2}-10x-12 & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-2{x}^{2}-10x-12$ lies **above** the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}-10x-12 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+10x+12 & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}+6x)+(4x+12) & =0 \\\\ 2x(x+3)+4(x+3) & =0 \\\\ (2x+4)(x+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-3$ and $x=-2,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/539e0e68f4a03c0bd4a309ebf2c4a00638d99c6eee233ca8f2cef3814e419c95.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}-10x-12>0,\n$$\n\n \nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-3<x<-2.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-3,-2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50c6f502bd60fceea6148813148952d7c9f32825dff9e7c7a62692e856f6f20d"} {"question" "q-277671" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277671" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277671" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563