irst need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & >12x \\\\ {x}^{2}-12x & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y={x}^{2}-12x$ lies **above** the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-12x & =0 \\\\ x(x-12) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=0$ and $x=12,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/387b02ad3416b06b3f86f12c99b921800ab4b86f39be9da0fc48883952d366d2.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-12x>0,\n$$\n\n \nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x<0$ or $x>12.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-\\infty ,0)⋃(12,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50c6f502bd60fceea6148813148952d7c9f32825dff9e7c7a62692e856f6f20d"} {"question" "q-277664" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277664" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\infty"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277664" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277664" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277664" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277664" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $-{x}^{2}>-x-12$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2} & >-x-12 \\\\ -{x}^{2}+x+12 & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-{x}^{2}+x+12$ lies **above** the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+x+12 & =0 \\\\ -({x}^{2}-x-12) & =0 \\\\ -(x+3)(x-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-3$ and $x=4,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/32e9a7babfbe9132a3a3e18c2f1efcbc3a33cd59bccc02099c7045b3fc39ee75.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}+x+12>0,\n$$\n\n \nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-3<x<4.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-3,4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50c6f502bd60fceea6148813148952d7c9f32825dff9e7c7a62692e856f6f20d"} {"question" "q-277670" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277670" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277670" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "q-277670" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json" "file_sha256" "e24df0582909315adb72fd277f390f540723e960e189ef30bf731563e1ac64f6"} {"question" "e-5186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution of $x^2-2x-8 \\geq 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/example-5186.json" "file_sha256" "b4c7eaa25a60bf698545ede44a4ff6544e978978d801375715cda9265835616f"} {"question" "e-5186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\nx^2-2x-8 \\geq 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=x^2-2x-8\n$$\n\nlies *above* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x-8 & =0 \\\\ (x+2)(x-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=-2$ and $x=4,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/6e9eeff6caaad8efe92d4726c1f04175ed3023ea99b7990436597233ef2910df.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *above* the axis or touches this axis. \n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x \\leq -2$ or $x \\geq 4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/example-5186.json" "file_sha256" "b4c7eaa25a60bf698545ede44a4ff6544e978978d801375715cda9265835616f"} {"question" "e-9977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution of $-x^2 + 7 x - 10 \\leq 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/example-9977.json" "file_sha256" "777a454ad62988086613d2a5788852bf5cd894a3a8f376df118d0190e9d94a68"} {"question" "e-9977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n-x^2 + 7 x - 10 \\leq 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny = -x^2 + 7 x - 10\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+7x-10 & =0 \\\\ -({x}^{2}-7x+10) & =0 \\\\ -(x-2)(x-5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=2$ and $x = 5,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/13e108b6383e99c5840789389378fd58cd8704484296485cb6483112ecf4ae25.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x \\leq 2$ or $x \\geq 5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/example-9977.json" "file_sha256" "777a454ad62988086613d2a5788852bf5cd894a3a8f376df118d0190e9d94a68"} {"question" "e-5063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution of $2x^2-6 \\le -4x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/example-5063.json" "file_sha256" "fc69993839495e5ce4f4f513518453b0e9faf99a269e301726360132c04297d9"} {"question" "e-5063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-6 & \\le -4x \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+4x-6 & \\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x-3 & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=x^2+2x-3$ lies below the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x-3 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)(x+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=1$ and $x=-3,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/0fe5ab0d38cea340e2227157bf1d434a0fccbab153289db52106857530fbc4dc.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving\n\n$$\nx^2+2x-3 \\le 0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis.  \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-3 \\le x \\le 1.$  \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x \\in [-3,1].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/example-5063.json" "file_sha256" "fc69993839495e5ce4f4f513518453b0e9faf99a269e301726360132c04297d9"} {"question" "e-9936" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution of $2x^2 < -4x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/example-9936.json" "file_sha256" "42d77b0ef274783f0c5c8a847b447811c37da825b1f54717fa0482e661eef614"} {"question" "e-9936" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2} & <-4x \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+4x & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y = 2x^2 + 4x$ lies below the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+4x & =0 \\\\ 2x(x+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x = -2$ and $x = 0,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/936653d6efd2ff155768730d61af5b68924c48933fa81b77998a668b7691fa10.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n2x^2 + 4x \\lt 0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-2 < x < 0.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x \\in \\left(-2, 0\\right).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/example-9936.json" "file_sha256" "42d77b0ef274783f0c5c8a847b447811c37da825b1f54717fa0482e661eef614"}] "usage" {"q-3951" [] "e-9977" [] "e-5186" [] "e-9936" [] "q-70302" [] "e-5063" []} "basis" 1327 "retractions" [[17592186184777 :question/problem "Find the solution of $-x^{2} + 3x \\ge 0$."] [17592186184710 :question/problem "Find the solution of $2x^{2} - 12 \\le - 5x$."] [17592186184012 :question/problem "Find the solution of $x^2-2x-8 \\geq 0$."] [17592186184012 :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality\n\n$$\nx^2-2x-8 \\geq 0\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n$y=x^2-2x-8$\nlies *above* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} - 2x - 8 &= 0 \\\\\n(x + 2)(x - 4) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=-2$ and $x=4$, and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3833/Source/Images/d48ff6ef1caea411bdbfb5e32821a420.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *above* the axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is\n\n$$\nx \\leq -2\n$$\n\nor\n\n$$\nx \\geq 4\n$$"] [17592186184074 :question/problem "Find the solution of $-x^2 + 7 x - 10 \\leq 0$."] [17592186184074 :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality\n\n$$\n-x^2 + 7 x - 10 \\leq 0\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n\n$$\ny = -x^2 + 7 x - 10\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-x^{2} + 7x - 10 &= 0 \\\\\n- (x^{2} - 7x + 10) &= 0 \\\\\n- (x - 2)(x - 5) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=2$ and $x = 5$, and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3833/Source/Images/66589305706cca7f293953c16fb19690.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is\n\n$$\nx \\leq 2\n$$\n\nor\n\n$$\nx \\geq 5\n$$"] [17592186184010 :question/problem "Find the solution of $2x^2-6 \\le -4x$."] [17592186184010 :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2x^{2} - 6 & \\le - 4x \\\\ 2x^{2} + 4x - 6 & \\le 0 \\\\ x^{2} + 2x - 3 & \\le 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n\n$$\ny=x^2+2x-3\n$$\n\nlies below the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} + 2x - 3 &= 0 \\\\\n(x - 1)(x + 3) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=1$ and $x=-3$, and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3833/Source/Images/4927c4ddb9348af5ed197223c5719193.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving\n\n$$\nx^2+2x-3 \\le 0\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is\n\n$$\n-3 \\le x \\le 1\n$$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x \\in [-3,1]$."] [17592186184061 :question/problem "Find the solution of $2x^2 < -4x$."] [17592186184061 :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0$.\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2x^{2} & < - 4x \\\\ 2x^{2} + 4x & < 0\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n\n$$\ny = 2x^2 + 4x\n$$\n\nlies below the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x^{2} + 4x &= 0 \\\\\n2x(x + 2) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x = -2$ and $x = 0$, and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3833/Source/Images/bddb58670bbcb57b9f310b467227d839.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving\n$2x^2 + 4x \\lt 0$,\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-2 < x < 0$.\n\nUsing interval notation, we write\n\n$$\nx \\in \\left(-2, 0\\right)\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186183150 17592186183151 17592186183152 17592186183153 17592186183154 17592186183552 17592186183553 17592186183554 17592186183555 17592186183556] "immutable_fields" [[17592186183149 :answer-field/correct] [17592186183149 :answer-field/id] [17592186183149 :answer-field/key] [17592186183149 :answer-field/type] [17592186183551 :answer-field/correct] [17592186183551 :answer-field/id] [17592186183551 :answer-field/key] [17592186183551 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
